        "original_id": "019b2c4c-2e9a-52b5-9e44-894b146c8620",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: One Manhattan Square, Time Warner Center, Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project, 247 Cherry\n- Companies: Extell Development Company, The Related Companies, AREA Property Partners, Apollo Real Estate Advisors, Skidmore, Owings & Merrill\n- People: David Childs, Mustafa Kemal Abadan, Stephen M. Ross\n- Places: Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- One Manhattan Square, also known as 227 Cherry Street or 250 South Street, is a residential skyscraper project being developed by Extell Development Company in Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City.\n- One Manhattan Square will stand 80 stories or 850 feet above the street and may include a new supermarket in the tower base.\n- Time Warner Center was developed by The Related Companies and AREA Property Partners, formerly known as Apollo Real Estate Advisors.\n- Time Warner Center was designed by David Childs and Mustafa Kemal Abadan of Skidmore, Owings & Merrill as two 750-foot twin towers connected by a multi-story atrium with upscale retail shops.\n- 247 Cherry will be adjacent to One Manhattan Square.\n- Stephen M. Ross's company Related is best known for developing the Time Warner Center and the Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project, and Ross lives and works at the Time Warner Center.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fb874414-b682-506c-b8ad-29e707ce34f3",
        "text": "Page: One Manhattan Square. Sentence: One Manhattan Square (also known as 227 Cherry Street or 250 South Street) is a residential skyscraper project being developed by Extell Development Company in Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City.\nPage: One Manhattan Square. Sentence: The building will stand 80 stories or 850 feet (259 m) above the street, and will possibly have a new supermarket in the tower's base.\nPage: Time Warner Center. Sentence: Developed by The Related Companies and AREA Property Partners (formerly known as Apollo Real Estate Advisors), its design by David Childs and Mustafa Kemal Abadan of Skidmore, Owings & Merrill, consists of two 750 ft twin towers bridged by a multi-story atrium containing upscale retail shops.\nPage: 247 Cherry. Sentence: The building will be adjacent One Manhattan Square.\nPage: Stephen M. Ross. Sentence: Related is best known for developing the Time Warner Center, where Ross lives and works, as well as the Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project.",
